## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **`Object.create(null)`** as accumulator | Produces a null-prototype object, eliminating false key collisions with inherited properties like `constructor`, `toString`, `hasOwnProperty`. |
| **`Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call`** | Safe existence check that works even on null-prototype objects. |
| **Mirror `Array.prototype.map` signature** (`item, index, array`) | Consistent with native array callbacks; lets callers use the index without a wrapper. |
| **Guard clauses with `TypeError`** | Fail fast with a clear message rather than silently producing wrong output. |
| **`Object.create(null)` return type** | Callers can safely spread (`{ ...groupBy(...) }`) or iterate with `Object.entries` without prototype noise. |

