## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **`Object.create(null)`** | Avoids prototype pollution — keys like `"toString"` or `"constructor"` won't collide with inherited properties. |
| **`Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call`** | Safe existence check that works even on null-prototype objects. |
| **`reduce` over `forEach`** | Idiomatic accumulator pattern; the accumulator *is* the result, so no external variable is needed. |
| **Pass `index` and `array` to `keyFn`** | Mirrors the `Array.prototype.map` / `forEach` contract — callers can use position-based grouping without extra closures. |
| **Strict `TypeError` guards** | Fail fast with a clear message rather than silently returning `{}` or producing `NaN`-keyed buckets. |
| **Generic types `T` and `K`** | The JSDoc generics make the function fully type-safe when consumed from TypeScript via `@ts-check`. |

