## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| `Object.create(null)` as accumulator | Avoids key collisions with `Object.prototype` properties (`constructor`, `toString`, etc.) |
| `keyFn(item, index, array)` signature | Mirrors `Array.prototype.map` — familiar and allows index-based grouping |
| Separate `groupByMap` function | Keeps the common case simple while providing an escape hatch for non-string keys |
| Guard clauses with `TypeError` | Fails fast with a clear message rather than a cryptic runtime error deep in `reduce` |
| Keys in insertion order | Both plain objects (ES2015+) and `Map` preserve insertion order, making output predictable |

# `groupBy` Utility Function

## Implementation

```javascript
/**
 * Groups an array of items into an object (or Map) keyed by a value
 * derived from each item via a callback function.
 *
 * @template T        - The type of items in the input array.
 * @template K        - The type of the derived key (string | number | symbol).
 *
 * @param {T[]} arr
 *   The array of items to group. Empty arrays return an empty object.
 *   `null` / `undefined` items are included and passed to `keyFn` as-is.
 *
 * @param {(item: T, index: number, array: T[]) => K} keyFn
 *   A pure function that receives each item (plus its index and the full
 *   array, mirroring the signature of `Array.prototype.map`) and returns
 *   the key under which that item should be grouped.
 *
 *   - Returning the same key for multiple items places them in the same group.
 *   - Returning `undefined` or `null` is allowed; those become literal string
 *     keys `"undefined"` / `"null"` in the plain-object result.
 *   - Throwing inside `keyFn` propagates normally – no items are silently dropped.
 *
 * @returns {Record<K, T[]>}
 *   A plain object whose keys are the distinct values returned by `keyFn`
 *   and whose values are arrays of items that produced that key, **in the
 *   same order they appeared in the original array**.
 *
 * @throws {TypeError} If `arr` is not an array or `keyFn` is not a function.
 *
 * @example
 * // ── Basic grouping ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * const people = [
 *   { name: 'Alice', dept: 'Engineering' },
 *   { name: 'Bob',   dept: 'Design'      },
 *   { name: 'Carol', dept: 'Engineering' },
 * ];
 *
 * groupBy(people, p => p.dept);
 * // {
 * //   Engineering: [{ name: 'Alice', … }, { name: 'Carol', … }],
 * //   Design:      [{ name: 'Bob',   … }],
 * // }
 *
 * @example
 * // ── Numeric keys ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * groupBy([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], n => n % 3);
 * // { '1': [1, 4], '2': [2, 5], '0': [3, 6] }
 *
 * @example
 * // ── Using index ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * groupBy(['a', 'b', 'c', 'd'], (_, i) => (i % 2 === 0 ? 'even' : 'odd'));
 * // { even: ['a', 'c'], odd: ['b', 'd'] }
 *
 * @example
 * // ── Nested key ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * const orders = [
 *   { id: 1, status: 'shipped',   region: 'US' },
 *   { id: 2, status: 'pending',   region: 'EU' },
 *   { id: 3, status: 'shipped',   region: 'EU' },
 * ];
 *
 * groupBy(orders, o => `${o.status}::${o.region}`);
 * // {
 * //   'shipped::US': [{ id: 1, … }],
 * //   'pending::EU': [{ id: 2, … }],
 * //   'shipped::EU': [{ id: 3, … }],
 * // }
 */
function groupBy(arr, keyFn) {
  // ── Guard clauses ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  if (!Array.isArray(arr)) {
    throw new TypeError(`groupBy: expected an array as the first argument, got ${typeof arr}`);
  }
  if (typeof keyFn !== 'function') {
    throw new TypeError(`groupBy: expected a function as the second argument, got ${typeof keyFn}`);
  }

  // ── Core reduction ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  return arr.reduce((groups, item, index) => {
    const key = keyFn(item, index, arr);

    // Avoid prototype-pollution: skip keys that shadow Object.prototype
    if (key === '__proto__' || key === 'constructor' || key === 'prototype') {
      throw new TypeError(`groupBy: key "${String(key)}" is not allowed (prototype pollution risk)`);
    }

    // If the bucket doesn't exist yet, create it; then push the item.
    if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(groups, key)) {
      groups[key].push(item);
    } else {
      groups[key] = [item];
    }

    return groups;
  }, Object.create(null)); // null-prototype object avoids inherited-key collisions
}
```

