## Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **`Map` as backing store** | Supports any value as a key, preserves insertion order, and has O(1) lookups. |
| **Lazy expiry** | Entries are only removed when accessed, avoiding the overhead of a background timer for small caches. |
| **`ttl: 0` means "no expiry"** | Provides a clean escape hatch to opt out of the instance default for a specific entry. |
| **`set` returns `this`** | Enables fluent chaining without sacrificing readability. |
| **`delete` mirrors `Map.delete`** | Returns a boolean so callers can distinguish a successful removal from a no-op. |

