## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **Jitter on by default** | Prevents [thundering herd](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thundering_herd_problem) when many clients retry simultaneously |
| **`Retry-After` header respected** | Servers (especially rate-limiters) signal the correct wait time — ignoring it wastes retries |
| **4xx not retried by default** | Client errors (bad request, unauthorized) won't fix themselves; only transient server errors are retried |
| **Custom `FetchRetryError`** | Preserves `attempts` count and root `cause` for structured error handling and logging |
| **Input validation** | Fails fast with clear messages instead of cryptic downstream errors |

