## Backoff Timing Reference

| Attempt | Formula                        | Example (base=300ms, no jitter cap) |
|---------|--------------------------------|--------------------------------------|
| 1st retry | `300 × 2⁰ = 300ms` + jitter | 0–300ms |
| 2nd retry | `300 × 2¹ = 600ms` + jitter | 0–600ms |
| 3rd retry | `300 × 2² = 1200ms` + jitter | 0–1200ms |
| 4th retry | `300 × 2³ = 2400ms` + jitter | 0–2400ms |
| 5th retry | `300 × 2⁴ = 4800ms` + jitter | 0–4800ms |

> **Full jitter** (`delay × Math.random()`) is used per [AWS recommendations](https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/architecture/exponential-backoff-and-jitter/) to prevent synchronized retries across many clients.

---

## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **Full jitter** | Prevents thundering herd — clients retry at spread-out times |
| **`AbortError` not retried** | Abort is intentional; retrying would violate caller intent |
| **4xx not retried by default** | Client errors are usually permanent (bad request, auth failure) |
| **`maxDelay` cap** | Prevents multi-minute waits in high-retry scenarios |
| **`FetchRetryError`** | Structured error preserves attempt count and root cause for debugging |
| **`onRetry` callback** | Decouples observability — caller controls logging/metrics |

# `fetchWithRetry` - Fetch with Exponential Backoff Retry

## Overview

A robust wrapper around the native `fetch` API that automatically retries failed requests using exponential backoff with jitter, preventing thundering herd problems in distributed systems.

```javascript
/**
 * Fetches a URL with automatic retry logic using exponential backoff.
 *
 * Retry behavior:
 * - Retries on network errors (no response received)
 * - Retries on configurable HTTP status codes (default: 408, 429, 500, 502, 503, 504)
 * - Uses exponential backoff: delay = baseDelay * 2^attempt + random jitter
 * - Respects Retry-After headers when present (429/503 responses)
 *
 * @param {string|URL}  url                          - The URL to fetch.
 * @param {RequestInit} [options={}]                 - Standard fetch options (method, headers, body, etc.).
 * @param {object}      [retryOptions={}]            - Configuration for retry behavior.
 * @param {number}      [retryOptions.retries=3]     - Maximum number of retry attempts (not counting the initial request).
 * @param {number}      [retryOptions.baseDelay=300] - Base delay in milliseconds before the first retry.
 * @param {number}      [retryOptions.maxDelay=30000]- Maximum delay in milliseconds between retries.
 * @param {number}      [retryOptions.factor=2]      - Exponential backoff multiplication factor.
 * @param {number[]}    [retryOptions.retryOn=[408, 429, 500, 502, 503, 504]]
 *                                                   - HTTP status codes that should trigger a retry.
 * @param {Function}    [retryOptions.onRetry]       - Optional callback invoked before each retry.
 *                                                     Receives ({ attempt, retries, delay, error, response }).
 * @param {AbortSignal} [retryOptions.signal]        - Optional AbortSignal to cancel all retry attempts.
 *
 * @returns {Promise<Response>} Resolves with the first successful Response.
 *
 * @throws {RetryError}  When all attempts are exhausted. Contains the last error/response.
 * @throws {DOMException} When the request is aborted via AbortSignal (name: 'AbortError').
 *
 * @example
 * // Basic usage — 3 retries with default settings
 * const response = await fetchWithRetry('https://api.example.com/data');
 * const data = await response.json();
 *
 * @example
 * // POST request with custom retry settings and callback
 * const response = await fetchWithRetry(
 *   'https://api.example.com/submit',
 *   {
 *     method: 'POST',
 *     headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
 *     body: JSON.stringify({ key: 'value' }),
 *   },
 *   {
 *     retries: 5,
 *     baseDelay: 500,
 *     maxDelay: 15000,
 *     retryOn: [429, 500, 503],
 *     onRetry: ({ attempt, retries, delay, error, response }) => {
 *       console.warn(
 *         `Retry ${attempt}/${retries} in ${delay}ms`,
 *         error ?? `HTTP ${response.status}`
 *       );
 *     },
 *   }
 * );
 *
 * @example
 * // With AbortController for timeout / manual cancellation
 * const controller = new AbortController();
 * setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 10_000); // cancel after 10 s
 *
 * const response = await fetchWithRetry(
 *   'https://api.example.com/slow',
 *   {},
 *   { signal: controller.signal, retries: 4 }
 * );
 */

// ─── Custom Error ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/**
 * Thrown when fetchWithRetry exhausts all retry attempts.
 *
 * @property {number}         attempts  - Total attempts made (initial + retries).
 * @property {Error|null}     lastError - The last network-level Error, if any.
 * @property {Response|null}  lastResponse - The last HTTP Response, if any.
 */
class RetryError extends Error {
  /**
   * @param {string}        message
   * @param {object}        context
   * @param {number}        context.attempts
   * @param {Error|null}    context.lastError
   * @param {Response|null} context.lastResponse
   */
  constructor(message, { attempts, lastError, lastResponse }) {
    super(message);
    this.name = 'RetryError';
    this.attempts = attempts;
    this.lastError = lastError;
    this.lastResponse = lastResponse;
  }
}

// ─── Helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/**
 * Calculates the delay before the next retry attempt.
 *
 * Formula: min(baseDelay * factor^attempt, maxDelay) + random jitter (±10 %)
 *
 * @param {number} attempt   - Current attempt index (0-based).
 * @param {number} baseDelay - Base delay in ms.
 * @param {number} maxDelay  - Maximum delay cap in ms.
 * @param {number} factor    - Backoff multiplication factor.
 * @returns {number} Delay in milliseconds.
 */
function calculateBackoff(attempt, baseDelay, maxDelay, factor) {
  const exponential = baseDelay * Math.pow(factor, attempt);
  const capped = Math.min(exponential, maxDelay);
  // Add ±10 % jitter to spread retries across clients
  const jitter = capped * 0.1 * (Math.random() * 2 - 1);
  return Math.round(capped + jitter);
}

/**
 * Extracts a retry delay from the `Retry-After` response header.
 * Supports both delta-seconds ("120") and HTTP-date ("Wed, 21 Oct 2025 07:28:00 GMT").
 *
 * @param {Response} response - The HTTP response to inspect.
 * @returns {number|null} Delay in milliseconds, or null if the header is absent/unparseable.
 */
function parseRetryAfter(response) {
  const header = response.headers.get('Retry-After');
  if (!header) return null;

  const seconds = Number(header);
  if (!Number.isNaN(seconds)) {
    return seconds * 1_000;
  }

  const date = Date.parse(header);
  if (!Number.isNaN(date)) {
    return Math.max(0, date - Date.now());
  }

  return null;
}

/**
 * Returns a promise that resolves after `ms` milliseconds.
 * Rejects immediately if the provided AbortSignal fires during the wait.
 *
 * @param {number}            ms     - Milliseconds to wait.
 * @param {AbortSignal|null}  signal - Optional signal to cancel the sleep.
 * @returns {Promise<void>}
 */
function sleep(ms, signal = null) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    if (signal?.aborted) {
      return reject(new DOMException('Aborted', 'AbortError'));
    }

    const timer = setTimeout(resolve, ms);

    signal?.addEventListener('abort', () => {
      clearTimeout(timer);
      reject(new DOMException('Aborted', 'AbortError'));
    }, { once: true });
  });
}

// ─── Main Function ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

async function fetchWithRetry(url, options = {}, retryOptions = {}) {
  const {
    retries    = 3,
    baseDelay  = 300,
    maxDelay   = 30_000,
    factor     = 2,
    retryOn    = [408, 429, 500, 502, 503, 504],
    onRetry    = null,
    signal     = null,
  } = retryOptions;

  // Validate inputs early to surface configuration mistakes immediately
  if (typeof retries !== 'number' || retries < 0) {
    throw new TypeError('retryOptions.retries must be a non-negative number');
  }
  if (typeof baseDelay !== 'number' || baseDelay < 0) {
    throw new TypeError('retryOptions.baseDelay must be a non-negative number');
  }

  const totalAttempts = retries + 1; // initial request + N retries
  let lastError    = null;
  let lastResponse = null;

  for (let attempt = 0; attempt < totalAttempts; attempt++) {
    // Honour cancellation before every attempt (including the first)
    if (signal?.aborted) {
      throw new DOMException('Aborted', 'AbortError');
    }

    try {
      // Forward the caller's AbortSignal so individual fetches can be cancelled
      const fetchSignal = signal
        ? signal  // reuse directly — AbortController supports multiple listeners
        : undefined;

      const response = await fetch(url, { ...options, signal: fetchSignal });

      // ── Success path ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      if (!retryOn.includes(response.status)) {
        return response; // ✅ Return the successful response
      }

      // ── Retryable HTTP error ──────────────────────────────────────────────
      lastResponse = response;
      lastError    = null;

      // No retries left — break out and throw below
      if (attempt >= retries) break;

      // Prefer server-specified delay (e.g. rate-limiting), fall back to backoff
      const retryAfterMs = parseRetryAfter(response);
      const delay = retryAfterMs !== null
        ? Math.min(retryAfterMs, maxDelay)
        : calculateBackoff(attempt, baseDelay, maxDelay, factor);

      onRetry?.({ attempt: attempt + 1, retries, delay, error: null, response });
      await sleep(delay, signal);

    } catch (error) {
      // Re-throw abort errors immediately — no point retrying a cancelled request
      if (error.name === 'AbortError') throw error;

      // ── Network-level error (DNS failure, connection refused, timeout…) ───
      lastError    = error;
      lastResponse = null;

      if (attempt >= retries) break;

      const delay = calculateBackoff(attempt, baseDelay, maxDelay, factor);
      onRetry?.({ attempt: attempt + 1, retries, delay, error, response: null });
      await sleep(delay, signal);
    }
  }

  // ── All attempts exhausted ────────────────────────────────────────────────
  throw new RetryError(
    `fetchWithRetry failed after ${totalAttempts} attempt(s): ` +
    (lastError?.message ?? `HTTP ${lastResponse?.status}`),
    { attempts: totalAttempts, lastError, lastResponse }
  );
}
