## Retry Delay Schedule (default config)

| Attempt | Base delay | Cap    | Approx. wait |
|---------|-----------|--------|--------------|
| 1st retry | 300 ms × 2⁰ = 300 ms | 10 000 ms | ~300–360 ms |
| 2nd retry | 300 ms × 2¹ = 600 ms | 10 000 ms | ~600–720 ms |
| 3rd retry | 300 ms × 2² = 1 200 ms | 10 000 ms | ~1 200–1 440 ms |
| 4th retry | 300 ms × 2³ = 2 400 ms | 10 000 ms | ~2 400–2 880 ms |
| 5th retry | 300 ms × 2⁴ = 4 800 ms | 10 000 ms | ~4 800–5 760 ms |

> Jitter adds 0–20% of the capped delay to spread out concurrent retries.

---

## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **Jitter on backoff** | Prevents thundering-herd when many clients retry simultaneously |
| **4xx not retried (except 429)** | Client errors (bad request, auth) won't fix themselves with time |
| **`AbortError` propagates immediately** | Caller explicitly cancelled — retrying would be wrong |
| **`FetchRetryError` wraps original** | Preserves `lastError` and `lastResponse` for debugging |
| **`sleep` respects `AbortSignal`** | Cancellation works even during the wait between retries |
| **Config validated at entry** | Fail fast with clear messages rather than silent misbehavior |

